# Rust
/target

# Node / frontend
node_modules
web/dist
web/dist-perf
web/dist-ui
web/perf-results
web/pkg
web/test-results
web/.playwright
playwright-report

# Go: `go build ./...` drops the binary in server/
/server/server

# Basemap extract — regenerate with `just basemap` (~94 MB at z15)
web/public/basemap.pmtiles
# Basemap glyphs and sprites — fetch with `just basemap-assets` (~14 MB)
web/public/basemap-assets/

mutants.out/
# Real C-TRAN GTFS — licensed agency data, fetched for dogfood QA only (docs/TESTING.md)
testdata/ctran-gtfs.zip
# County roads export for the street soak (`just soak`, COUNTY_GEOJSON) — ~99 MB
testdata/CTRANTrapezeRoads_*.geojson
# Recorded live feeds for the perf runner (web/perf/record-rt.mjs)
testdata/perf-rt*/

# Build outputs of `just caps` (cap-abi gen-manifest): the hash-pinned
# modules, manifest, and demo fixtures the browser serves, and the
# published registry caps-run reads. Regenerated by every `just test`.
registry/
web/public/caps/

# The assembly crates (gen-assemblies, `just caps`): generated from the
# capability crates and each web/src/uis/<id>/ui.json, never committed
# (D-85). The .gitkeep keeps the directory, so the workspace glob
# (Cargo.toml `assemblies/*`) resolves in a fresh checkout.
assemblies/*
!assemblies/.gitkeep

# The TS bindings (ts-rs), generated from the Rust model by `just
# types` (which `just build` runs first) and by every cargo test run.
# Rust is the source of truth; the manifest's computed op examples are
# the readable wire contract.
web/src/types/

# ts-rs scatter: bindings land here when cargo runs without
# TS_RS_EXPORT_DIR. .cargo/config.toml points every run at
# web/src/types, so these never come back.
crates/*/bindings/

# The local geocoder (`just geocoder-build`): pelias/docker and its data
.pelias/
